 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "s2_p01",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How do I find the eigenvalues of a 2x2 matrix? I know it's det(A - λI) = 0 but I get lost after that.",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:02:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p02",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What does it mean geometrically that a vector is an eigenvector?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:04:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p03",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What's the difference between P(A|B) and P(B|A)? I always mix them up.",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:06:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p04",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "A test is 99% accurate and the disease has 1% prevalence. If I test positive, what's the chance I have it? I got 99% but that seems wrong.",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:08:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p05",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "When is a matrix diagonalizable? Is it enough that the eigenvalues are distinct?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:10:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p06",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What's the difference between an INNER JOIN and a LEFT JOIN?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:12:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p07",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Are independent events the same as mutually exclusive events?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:14:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p08",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How do I compute the rank of a matrix with row reduction?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:16:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p09",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "My LEFT JOIN returns more rows than the left table has. How is that possible?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:18:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p10",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Is the rank of A the same as the rank of A transpose? Why?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:20:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p11",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How do I compute the expected value of a die roll?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:22:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p12",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What is 3NF and how do I check if my schema is in it?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:24:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p13",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What's the difference between SVD and eigendecomposition?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:26:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p14",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Var(X+Y) = Var(X) + Var(Y), does that only hold if X and Y are independent?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:28:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p15",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c1",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "When should I add an index to a column?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:30:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p16",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How is SVD used for low-rank approximation of an image?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:32:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p17",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "When should I use a binomial vs a Poisson distribution?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:34:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p18",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "If a matrix has eigenvalue 0, does that mean it's not invertible?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:36:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p19",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Why is a B-tree index good for range queries but a hash index isn't?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:38:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p20",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Can you explain the law of total probability with an example?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:40:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p21",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "I diagonalized A = PDP^-1, how do I use that to compute A^10?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:42:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p22",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "How do I write a query that finds customers with no orders?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:44:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p23",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "What is a probability density function, and why can it be bigger than 1?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:46:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p24",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Is denormalization ever a good idea?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:48:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p25",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Is the number of nonzero singular values equal to the rank?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:50:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p26",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
   "role": "user",
   "text": "Bayes: prior, likelihood, posterior, which is which in the formula?",
   "createdAt": "2026-12-01T09:52:00Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "s2_p27",
   "conversationId": "s2_mixed:c2",
